umented deep vein thrombosis of the lower limb (with or without pulmonary embolism)\n-  Out-patients referred for clinically suspected acute recurrent ipsilateral DVT of the lower limb i.e. the occurrence of new symptoms and signs of DVT or the increase of symptoms and signs in patients with post-thrombotic syndrome\n-  Patients covered by social security or equivalent regimen\n-  Signed and dated informed consent\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Age >= 18 years",\n                  "Eq-Operator": [\n                    ">="\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n                    "years"\n                  ],\n                  "Age": [\n                    "Age"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Value": [\n                    "18"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Comparison": [\n                    ">= 18 years"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "OR": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "- Known history of objectively documented deep vein thrombosis of the lower limb (with or",\n                      "Eq-Operator": [\n                        "or"\n                      ],\n                      "Modifier": [\n                        "lower limb"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition": [\n                        "deep vein thrombosis"\n                      ],\n                      "Eq-Comparison": [\n                        "history"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition-Name": [\n                        "deep vein thrombosis"\n                      ],\n                      "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                        "history"\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    "right": {\